{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/7029-favorite-era","id":7029,"title":"Favorite era?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-09T14:22:07-08:00","id":7029,"title":"Favorite era?","content":"So, which of the three games of the setting is your favorite?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/373-infernal-teddy","name":"Infernal Teddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar373_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T23:06:02-08:00","id":7196,"title":"","content":"For me, it is no contest. Aberrant. I picked up Aeon and thought &quot;Hmmm, this is cute&quot; but my first love in rpg's will always be the superhero genre.<br /> <br /> I saw Aberrant and picked it up and read it and fell in love with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T04:36:51-08:00","id":7285,"title":"","content":"Trinitty. Because the idea of being out-gunned by a superpowered being, but still being able to taken em down with tenacity, cleverness etc etc... well it is just will a love action/thriller sci fi games as a whole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T04:52:58-08:00","id":7290,"title":"","content":"<b>Adventure! </b> Give me some good old-fashioned pulp adventure any day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T08:33:48-08:00","id":7366,"title":"","content":"Abberant. Superheroes &gt; Everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T10:42:41-08:00","id":7477,"title":"","content":"Aeon. The Psion is my favorite of the 3 heros.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T11:30:30-08:00","id":7529,"title":"","content":"ABERRANT is the Best of the Three...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/589-aberrant_scion","name":"ABERRANT_SCION","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T12:21:28-08:00","id":7558,"title":"","content":"I love Aeon, and Aberrant can be fun, but Adventure! will always rule my heart.<br /> <br /> -Slag","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T12:37:45-08:00","id":7577,"title":"","content":"Aberrant is probably my favorite to play. But, damn, that Trinity setting is soooo cool. I always wanted to run a game with recently erupted novas on Trinity-era Earth, trying to figure out what to do, avoid the authorities, Orders and Aeon...maybe eventually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T13:24:40-08:00","id":7620,"title":"","content":"While I love Trinity and have had great fun playing through the campaigns - nothing will every beat the awesomeness that is Adventure!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/68-42","name":"42!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar68_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T18:35:50-08:00","id":7799,"title":"","content":"Trinity, hands down. Psions, epic sci-fi setting covering space-opera to mad-max style post apocalypse, deep shades of grey with the powers that be. Yep, love it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T22:08:19-08:00","id":7874,"title":"","content":"Aberrant, although Adventure is an extremely close second.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/238-hammerofheaven","name":"HammerofHeaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar238_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T00:28:28-08:00","id":7916,"title":"","content":"For me Aberrant and Trinity are running neck and neck though Aberrant might be just a hair ahead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/869-bc001","name":"BC001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar869_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T16:13:20-08:00","id":8441,"title":"","content":"I actually enjoyed all three!!! A grand departure from the World of Darkness doom and gloom...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1023-marz-blaque","name":"Marz Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1023_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T05:05:18-08:00","id":8731,"title":"","content":"I'm torn, I wanted to like Aeon/Trinity more, but their view of the future and reduction of the Psion groups to TK=Millitary, Telepaths = Bureaucracy, Eletrokinetics= Big Bussiness, Healers= Souless Science and/or New Age Goofs, Biokinetics=Organised Crime, Teleporters=Survivalists, Clairsentiants=Mystic Religion,( and the Quantikinetics were probably Acedemic Phillosophy) were both boring and fustraiting. Abberant was fun, inspite of the gloom. Adventure!, because it embraced pleasure and hope, was the best of the lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T07:11:14-08:00","id":8779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/7029-favorite-era?p=8731#post8731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm torn, I wanted to like Aeon/Trinity more, but their view of the future and reduction of the Psion groups to TK=Millitary, Telepaths = Bureaucracy, Eletrokinetics= Big Bussiness, Healers= Souless Science and/or New Age Goofs, Biokinetics=Organised Crime, Teleporters=Survivalists, Clairsentiants=Mystic Religion,( and the Quantikinetics were probably Acedemic Phillosophy) were both boring and fustraiting. Abberant was fun, inspite of the gloom. Adventure!, because it embraced pleasure and hope, was the best of the lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never played the original Aeon/Trinity but, and this was probably not the intended effect, you just sold me on the idea. Everything you said in that post sounded very interesting and fun.<br /> <br /> Sorry for being contrairian, It's just that everything you said you didn't like sounds so fun. a psychic based caste society sounds pretty freaking cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T07:59:55-08:00","id":8811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/7029-favorite-era?p=8779#post8779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It's just that everything you said you didn't like sounds so fun. a psychic based caste society sounds pretty freaking cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dirt cheap on Drivethru right now: <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/3407/Trinity-Rulebook?cPath=8329_8567&amp;it=1\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/produc...8329_8567&amp;it=1</a><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T16:51:02-08:00","id":9304,"title":"","content":"I admit the comic book geek in me loved Aberrant and the Sci fi geek in me loved Trinity. That is why I am definitely interested in what other genres could be explored with this universe. The reason Trinity was my favorite of the two was partly because the world was a psychic based caste society.which I thought was very unique at the time","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/601-dioscuri","name":"Dioscuri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T04:28:36-08:00","id":11167,"title":"","content":"Hey Xiongrey, if I helped you find something good for you, I'm proud to have helped.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T08:03:51-08:00","id":12074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/7029-favorite-era?p=8779#post8779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never played the original Aeon/Trinity but, and this was probably not the intended effect, you just sold me on the idea. Everything you said in that post sounded very interesting and fun.<br /> <br /> Sorry for being contrairian, It's just that everything you said you didn't like sounds so fun. a psychic based caste society sounds pretty freaking cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is cool; the setting depth is rich and the reasons behind the setup make sense given the state of society when the Orders were originally formed. The roles are not rigid either, one of the PCs in a campaign I ran was a clairvoyant (actually a teleporter posing as one, but that is another story) who was a member of the Legion who used her position-sense to good effect as an artillery spotter/scout for instance. While each particular Order has a traditional role individual members mix around to some degree because the organizations need things done that can be done better with the abilities of another Order and hire some to do them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/869-bc001","name":"BC001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar869_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T18:29:14-08:00","id":13096,"title":"","content":"Adventure! There are plenty of better Super hero games and settings out there, and Aeon was never able to hold my interest. Adventure just drew me in, held my interest and keeps calling back to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T18:52:34-08:00","id":13113,"title":"","content":"I love what you can do with Aberrant and its themes about power and celebrity culture. It needs major revisions for how it presents geopolitics and post-N-Day history to be taken seriously now though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T09:19:33-08:00","id":13434,"title":"","content":"I had not really heard of these until like yesterday. I'm really happy to see that it's roughly balanced between the three eras.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1071-raleel","name":"Raleel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T13:43:57-08:00","id":16262,"title":"","content":"I preferred the ruleset from Adventure, but I preferred the setting from Abberant. With Aventure I was more likely to pick something and run with it, creating a crazy adventure shifting from goofy to dark as needed, whereas with Abberant I tended to hew a lot closer to the established metaplot and let the players dig into dark corners of the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Remember - popcorn can feel pain.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1195-frivyeti","name":"FrivYeti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T17:39:59-08:00","id":16356,"title":"","content":"<i>Adventure!</i> was my favorite of the lot.<br /> <br /> And stuff","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T10:28:40-08:00","id":17177,"title":"","content":"I like a lot of world-building, and (aside from the obvious changes) Aberrant always seemed a bit too much &quot;the world outside your window&quot;, cool as it was. Adventure! had the distinction of being a more &quot;exotic&quot; time period, AND having lost civilizations and the like, which was better. But Trinity absolutely took the cake for me!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T13:51:05-08:00","id":17285,"title":"","content":"i agree glamweaver. The Governments Anti-Nova-ness should be more of a focus in the mainbook. Though the Media will be obessed with them too... To bad 99% of people will only see the Media obession...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/589-aberrant_scion","name":"ABERRANT_SCION","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T15:02:23-08:00","id":17326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ABERRANT_SCION</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/7029-favorite-era?p=17285#post17285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i agree glamweaver. The Governments Anti-Nova-ness should be more of a focus in the mainbook. Though the Media will be obessed with them too... To bad 99% of people will only see the Media obession...</div> </div> </div> </div>That's all fine (though most governments have a more nuanced pov on novas - of wanting to harness them rather than being strictly against them). Mostly I meant stuff from the original books that really show their age now. It's very clearly an AMERICAN post-Cold-War pre-9/11 view of geopolitics.<br /> <br /> I'd like to see the new Aberrant book fetishize Japan less, make China a much bigger player (I'd say make the Directive represent the 5 permanent Security Council members, for example), completely rewrite the UK &amp; Ireland stuff, which was just embarrassingly wrong last time (the author of the Directive book seriously didn't understand that South Ireland was 0% part of the UK), don't grossly oversimplify Islam into pro-Nova Sufis (who somehow completely supplant Salafi Islam and dominate Sunni identity) and anti-Nova Shia...<br /> <br /> Do we also need to do the ridiculous Libertarian President thing? That just always jumped out at me as one author's personal fantasy rather than anything remotely reasonable in the setting.<br /> <br /> Do we know if the new edition is leaving N-Day in 1998 and making the &quot;present&quot; 2008? I'd actually suggest moving N-Day to 2008 (perhaps tied to the activation of the LHC, and making the economic collapse the following week the panic enhanced aftermath....)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T07:10:22-08:00","id":18387,"title":"","content":"I've only ever run Aeon/Trinity and played in Aberrant and Adventure! Our Adventure! game didn't last long but it was my favorite. The largest and most extensive background I ever wrote for a character was for that game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=485\" data-tempid=\"temp_485_1538393298974_786\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1277-karpomatic","name":"karpomatic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1277_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T13:25:08-07:00","id":201406,"title":"","content":"The Aberrant era was deffinitely m favorite. liked the subversion of the superhero genre, the mix of wonder, hope and hidden darkness. I also absolutely loved how the impact of novas on society was treated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T15:21:10-07:00","id":201509,"title":"","content":"Aberrant for sure. Then Trinity, Adventure doesn't really interest me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T20:07:10-07:00","id":201737,"title":"","content":"Aberrant then Adventure and finally Trinity though thanks to awesomeness of Aberrant I can never quite enjoy Trinity as much as I probably should.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T09:21:46-07:00","id":202202,"title":"","content":"I like them three but my selection is. Adventure&gt;Aberrant&gt;Aeon. What can I say? I'm a romantic adventurer in my heart. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T11:32:20-07:00","id":202279,"title":"","content":"Aberrant, for me. Adventure wins out in terms of the writing and feel, but I like the deconstruction of superhero settings enough for Aberrant to edge out.<br /> <br /> I don't really care much for Psions, so my only interest in a Trinity era game would be exploring what's going on with the nova diaspora.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T21:29:06-07:00","id":202633,"title":"","content":"I love Aberrant dearly, because I dearly live getting to deal with issues of tremendous power and celebrity and spirituality and redirecting the course of human history...but at the end of the day?<br /> <br /> Adventure has underground cities of intelligent apes and an island of giant carnivorous plants and it has a mad German scientist who is building floating cities on giant zeppelins in the upper atmosphere and it has zombies and races to beat Nazis to recover the Ancient Egyptian Laser Beam and it's got old school sexism and racism for you to build drama out of and there's a secret ancient martial art that makes you enemies go blind and rules for making giant steampunk submarines and huge insectoid mechanisms armed with Death Rays because nobody has invented lasers yet and oh god they have biplanes and there are snake men who are trying to resurrect their dead god and they are FISTFIGHTING on TOP of the biplanes while there's an aerial dogfight and meanwhile some scientist has just discovered a cure for old age but he needs a rare orchid to synthesize it and he's funding a secret expedition into the depths of the steaming Amazon to face the jaguar-demons who guard the ancient temple where it grows and did I mention that men from the moon are using hypnosis to force a group of former WW1 veterans who now run a circus together to kidnap the brilliant scientist's beautiful daughter to black nail him into building a giant robot warrior for their mad queen, who plots to conquer the hidden aquatic empire of Atlantis!<br /> <br /> And that's just, like...the first three sessions? Seriously, I love the Inspiration mechanics and the setting, but at the end of the day I love Adventure for the ridiculous amount of absolute crack I can cram into a game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 07-20-2014, 05:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T18:35:18-07:00","id":271281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/7029-favorite-era?p=202633#post202633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love Aberrant dearly, because I dearly live getting to deal with issues of tremendous power and celebrity and spirituality and redirecting the course of human history...but at the end of the day?<br /> <br /> Adventure has underground cities of intelligent apes and an island of giant carnivorous plants and it has a mad German scientist who is building floating cities on giant zeppelins in the upper atmosphere and it has zombies and races to beat Nazis to recover the Ancient Egyptian Laser Beam and it's got old school sexism and racism for you to build drama out of and there's a secret ancient martial art that makes you enemies go blind and rules for making giant steampunk submarines and huge insectoid mechanisms armed with Death Rays because nobody has invented lasers yet and oh god they have biplanes and there are snake men who are trying to resurrect their dead god and they are FISTFIGHTING on TOP of the biplanes while there's an aerial dogfight and meanwhile some scientist has just discovered a cure for old age but he needs a rare orchid to synthesize it and he's funding a secret expedition into the depths of the steaming Amazon to face the jaguar-demons who guard the ancient temple where it grows and did I mention that men from the moon are using hypnosis to force a group of former WW1 veterans who now run a circus together to kidnap the brilliant scientist's beautiful daughter to black nail him into building a giant robot warrior for their mad queen, who plots to conquer the hidden aquatic empire of Atlantis!<br /> <br /> And that's just, like...the first three sessions? Seriously, I love the Inspiration mechanics and the setting, but at the end of the day I love Adventure for the ridiculous amount of absolute crack I can cram into a game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plus, Adventure! Is the most hopeful of the three, in my opinion. You are the first &quot;supers&quot; of the modern age. No other groups have come before you, you aren't destined to go insane, and the aforementioned destined to go insane individuals aren't trying to destroy the universe you're trying to protect. So long as you tell the metaplot to beat it, you can really change the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T19:07:04-07:00","id":273407,"title":"","content":"I love them all, but I suppose Adventure is my favorite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T08:52:02-07:00","id":273898,"title":"","content":"I love them all too, but Aberrant got the most play out of us...a full year of a weekly playgroup! That's a record for us!<br /> <br /> But I really wanted to see more done with Adventure! Pulp is such a cool genre, but doesn't seem to get the supplements it deserves. At least I found Hollow Earth Expeditions and Spirit of the Century to fill that void. =)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3194-midnightblue","name":"MidnightBlue","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}